  "qualifications": [
    "The extracted source oracle uses an explicit fixed named-token resolver for <named>, <s> and </s>; resolution must return exactly one token as in the original parser.",
    "Only assertion/abort/logging boundaries are replaced in the oracle wrapper, to report failures without ending the harness; the 31 grammar functions remain unchanged.",
    "Negative acceptance is tested on a clone, which is discarded after the original exception. Rust additionally preserves state transactionally on its error.",
    "Lazy regex/word triggering is owned by the sampler layer and is excluded from this direct engine fixture.",
    "Invalid repetition ranges with maximum smaller than minimum are rejected by Rust and excluded from native execution; the original would attempt an enormous allocation."
  ],
